# The character runtime folder (index.json and files/, ASSETS.md). Unset, it is
# ./runtime, where bin/fetch-runtime installs the release this checkout pins
# (bin/dev runs it when the folder is missing or stale). Set it to use another
# folder, such as the maker's own prepared runtime/. Relative paths resolve from
# this game checkout; never a VITE_* variable. Restart Vite after editing.
# VANAI_RUNTIME=../vanai_assets_maker/runtime

# PostgreSQL. Development connects as your OS user over the local socket
# (README "Getting started"). For another role or server, export libpq's own
# variables in your shell before bin/dev -- Rails does not read this file:
#   export PGHOST=localhost PGUSER=vanai PGPASSWORD=secret
# Prefer them to DATABASE_URL, which would also replace the test database, so
# `bin/rails test` would empty your development data.
